new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ac087a7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Consulted live sources
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14.
+
+- Broadcom Compatibility Guide, “VMware Cloud Foundation” and “vSAN ReadyNode” compatibility material, https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/. Consulted to confirm that both candidate profiles require release-compatible certified hardware and networking; for this comparison ESA uses four 25 GbE ports while OSA uses two shared 10 GbE ports.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base 440630, “Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1,” https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html. Consulted for the VCF Operations-first requirement and the supported lifecycle path from VCF 5.2.x to 9.1.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base 448135, “Upgrade failure for vCenter 8.0 U3j, ESXi 8.0 U3j, and NSX 4.2.4 due to back-in-time restriction,” https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/448135/upgrade-failure-for-vcenter-80-u3j-esxi.html. Consulted to confirm the VCF 9.1.0.0 target combination of NSX `9.1.0.0.25318225`, vCenter `9.1.0.0.25370922`, and ESXi `9.1.0.0.25370933`, plus the interoperability/back-in-time precheck requirement.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base 317674, “vSAN Health Service - Hardware compatibility - Physical NIC link speed is satisfied to the minimum requirements,” https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/317674/vsan-health-service-hardware-compatibil.html. Consulted to confirm that vSAN ESA recommends at least 25 Gbps of aggregate network connectivity and validates the physical NIC link speed.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base 432894, “How to convert a vSAN OSA (Original Storage Architecture) cluster to an ESA (Express Storage Architecture) cluster,” https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/432894/how-to-convert-a-vsan-osa-original-stora.html. Consulted to confirm there is no direct in-place OSA-to-ESA conversion: an empty certified ESA cluster is built side-by-side, workloads move with Storage vMotion, and OSA is decommissioned only after workload validation.
